/-!
# Hereditary C⋆-subalgebras, closed left ideals, and hereditary cones

A `⋆`-subalgebra `B` of a C⋆-algebra `A` is *hereditary* (`TauCeti.CStarAlgebra.IsHereditary`) if
`0 ≤ a ≤ b` and `b ∈ B` imply `a ∈ B`. When `B` is norm-closed, order heredity is equivalent to
the multiplicative sandwich condition `B * A * B ⊆ B`
(`NonUnitalStarSubalgebra.isHereditary_iff_mul_mem`; the forward implication requires no closedness
hypothesis, `TauCeti.CStarAlgebra.IsHereditary.mul_mem`).

For any self-adjoint (in particular, positive) element `a : A`, the closure of the algebraic corner
`{a * x * a | x : A}` is the least closed hereditary `⋆`-subalgebra of `A` containing `a`
(`TauCeti.CStarAlgebra.hereditarySubalgebra`).

Closed hereditary `⋆`-subalgebras of `A`, closed complex left ideals of `A`, and closed hereditary
cones inside the positive cone `A₊` stand in order-preserving bijection:
* `B ↦ {x : A | star x * x ∈ B}` and `L ↦ L ∩ star ⁻¹' L`
  (`TauCeti.CStarAlgebra.hereditarySubalgebraOrderIsoClosedLeftIdeal`);
* `B ↦ B ∩ A₊` and `P ↦ {x : A | star x * x ∈ P ∧ x * star x ∈ P}`
  (`TauCeti.CStarAlgebra.hereditarySubalgebraOrderIsoProperCone`).

Moreover, by right-module Cohen–Hewitt factorization over an approximate unit of `B`, the left
ideal `{x : A | star x * x ∈ B}` coincides with the set product `Set.univ * (B : Set A)`
(`NonUnitalStarSubalgebra.coe_closedLeftIdeal_eq_univ_mul`).

## Main declarations

* `TauCeti.CStarAlgebra.IsHereditary`: order-heredity predicate `0 ≤ a → a ≤ b → b ∈ s → a ∈ s`
  on any `SetLike` carrier, with `isHereditary_iff_ordConnected` and
  `isHereditary_iff_ordConnected_of_nonneg`.
* `TauCeti.CStarAlgebra.IsHereditary.mul_mem` and
  `NonUnitalStarSubalgebra.isHereditary_iff_mul_mem`: the `B * A * B ⊆ B` sandwich characterization
  of closed hereditary `⋆`-subalgebras.
* `TauCeti.CStarAlgebra.hereditarySubalgebra`: the closed hereditary `⋆`-subalgebra `closure(aAa)`
  generated by a self-adjoint element `a`, with `self_mem_hereditarySubalgebra` and universal
  property `hereditarySubalgebra_le_iff`.
* `ProperCone.leftIdeal`, `ClosedSubmodule.isHereditary_starSubalgebra`,
  `ClosedSubmodule.isHereditary_of_mul_mem`, `NonUnitalStarSubalgebra.positiveCone`, and
  `NonUnitalStarSubalgebra.closedLeftIdeal`: the maps linking hereditary cones, closed complex left
  ideals (with self-adjoint core `ClosedSubmodule.starSubalgebra`), and closed hereditary
  `⋆`-subalgebras, packaged as order isomorphisms
  `TauCeti.CStarAlgebra.hereditarySubalgebraOrderIsoClosedLeftIdeal` and
  `TauCeti.CStarAlgebra.hereditarySubalgebraOrderIsoProperCone`.
* `NonUnitalStarSubalgebra.exists_mul_eq_of_star_mul_self_mem` and
  `NonUnitalStarSubalgebra.coe_closedLeftIdeal_eq_univ_mul`: Cohen–Hewitt factorization identifying
  `{x : A | star x * x ∈ B}` with `Set.univ * B`.

## References

* B. Blackadar, *Operator Algebras: Theory of C⋆-Algebras and von Neumann Algebras*,
  II.5.3.1, II.5.3.2, and II.5.3.7.
* G. J. Murphy, *C⋆-Algebras and Operator Theory*, Section 3.2, Theorem 3.2.2.
* G. K. Pedersen, *C⋆-Algebras and their Automorphism Groups*, Section 1.5.
-/

